JWasm: -Zj keys the pass one instruction sizes by source position

Patch 0002 records the size of each instruction in pass one and pads it
with NOPs in later passes, matching each instruction to pass one's by
its index in the instruction sequence. With STRUC.INC, the sequence is
not the same in pass two (a JMP becomes JMP SHORT and NOP, labels are
renamed, IF1 code drops out), and every instruction after the first
difference lost its padding.

Each recorded size is now keyed by the instruction's position: the
source file, its inclusion number in the pass (a file can be included
more than once), the line (a macro's instructions are at the line that
invoked it), the instruction's text (mnemonic and whether it says SHORT)
and its occurrence number among the same instructions of that line.
Later passes look the position up in a hash table and pad only the same
instruction.

